I added a streaming Server-Sent Events endpoint at `GET /sse` to the RedwoodSDK app.

## Changes

In `src/worker.tsx`, I added an `sseStream()` helper that builds a `ReadableStream<Uint8Array>` and a `route("/sse", { get: ... })` entry in the `defineApp` array (placed before the `render(Document, ...)` block so it returns a raw streaming `Response` rather than an HTML document).

## Implementation

```typescript
function sseStream(): ReadableStream<Uint8Array> {
  const encoder = new TextEncoder();

  return new ReadableStream<Uint8Array>({
    start(controller) {
      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        const data = JSON.stringify({ index: i, message: `tick-${i}` });
        const event =
          `id: ${i}\n` + `data: ${data}\n` + `\n`;
        controller.enqueue(encoder.encode(event));
      }

      // Terminal event signaling the end of the stream.
      const doneEvent = `event: done\n` + `data: [DONE]\n` + `\n`;
      controller.enqueue(encoder.encode(doneEvent));

      controller.close();
    },
  });
}

export default defineApp([
  setCommonHeaders(),
  ({ ctx }) => { ctx; },
  route("/sse", {
    get: () => {
      return new Response(sseStream(), {
        headers: {
          "Content-Type": "text/event-stream",
          "Cache-Control": "no-cache",
          Connection: "keep-alive",
        },
      });
    },
  }),
  render(Document, [route("/", Home)]),
]);
```

It uses only standard Web APIs (`ReadableStream` / `TextEncoder`) compatible with the Cloudflare Workers runtime.

## Verification

Running `curl -s -N -i http://localhost:5173/sse` produced the expected wire output:

```
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
content-type: text/event-stream
cache-control: no-cache
Connection: keep-alive

id: 0
data: {"index":0,"message":"tick-0"}

id: 1
data: {"index":1,"message":"tick-1"}

id: 2
data: {"index":2,"message":"tick-2"}

id: 3
data: {"index":3,"message":"tick-3"}

id: 4
data: {"index":4,"message":"tick-4"}

event: done
data: [DONE]

```

All requirements are met:
- ✅ `GET /sse` returns a streaming `Response` speaking the SSE protocol
- ✅ Headers: `Content-Type: text/event-stream`, `Cache-Control: no-cache`, `Connection: keep-alive`
- ✅ Exactly 5 message events with zero-based `id:` lines and compact JSON `data:` lines of shape `{"index":<n>,"message":"tick-<n>"}`
- ✅ One terminal `event: done` event with `data: [DONE]`
- ✅ Every event terminated by a blank line (`\n\n`)
- ✅ The stream closes on its own after the terminal event (server ends it; the client does not need to abort)
- ✅ `tsc --noEmit` passes with no type errors
